flow "Lamport logical clocks"
summary "Orders causally linked events across machines with a single integer counter, while illustrating why timestamps alone cannot detect concurrency."
tags clocks causality ordering
level intermediate
source "https://lamport.azurewebsites.net/pubs/time-clocks.pdf"
related distributed-systems/vector-clocks

node a "Node A" service tone=primary
node b "Node B" service
node c "Node C" service
edge a > b
edge b > c
edge a > c
array clk "Lamport counter L" keys=a,b,c = 0 0 0

scenario order "Happens-before guarantees L(a) < L(b)"
  step a-event "Node A performs local event e1"
    "Physical wall clocks drift, so Lamport clocks count **events** instead of seconds. Before any local event or send, Node A increments its counter: `L(A) = 1`."
    state a active
    label clk#a "1"
    state clk#a active with
  step a-to-b "Node A sends (m1, t=1) to Node B"
    "Every message carries the sender's timestamp. On receipt, Node B applies `L = max(L, t) + 1 = max(0, 1) + 1 = 2`."
    send a > b "m1 (t=1)"
    label clk#b "2"
    state b,clk#b active with
  step b-to-c "Node B sends (m2, t=2) to Node C"
    "Node B forwards its causal successor `m2 (t=2)`. Node C jumps to `max(0, 2) + 1 = 3`, preserving `e1 -> e2 -> e3 => 1 < 2 < 3`."
    send b > c "m2 (t=2)"
    label clk#c "3"
    state a,b,c,clk success with
    callout c "Causal chain: 1 < 2 < 3"

scenario out-of-order "Out-of-order message and concurrency limit" from=order/a-event
  step b-runs-ahead "Node B executes 4 local events first"
    "While A's message `(t=1)` is delayed in the network, Node B processes four local events, advancing its clock to `L(B) = 4`."
    state b active
    label clk#b "4"
    state clk#b active with
  step late-msg "Delayed message (t=1) arrives at Node B"
    "A's delayed message `(t=1)` finally reaches B. Using `max(4, 1) + 1 = 5`, Node B never moves its clock backwards."
    send a > b "late m1 (t=1)"
    label clk#b "5"
    state b,clk#b warning with
    callout b "max(4, 1) + 1 = 5 (monotonic)"
  step no-converse "L(a) < L(b) does NOT prove causality"
    "Notice that `L(e1)=1 < L(B's 4th event)=4`, even though those two events were completely independent! Lamport clocks give a partial order only one way; use **vector clocks** to detect concurrency."
    focus a,b dim
    callout a "1 < 4, yet A and B were concurrent"
